        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "753cad07-f032-3995-a9fc-c4ae11d3edc6",
                "word": "échappatoire",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a4e9e44e-0647-4783-82ea-4dad164a150c",
                        "entry_id": "753cad07-f032-3995-a9fc-c4ae11d3edc6",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "échappatoires"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0d9e5229-00a4-314b-b399-951b8dae1e11",
                        "entry_id": "753cad07-f032-3995-a9fc-c4ae11d3edc6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Subterfuge, moyen habile pour se tirer d’embarras."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c96c0c1-70b4-4b11-9e72-578953571a36",
                                "sense_id": "0d9e5229-00a4-314b-b399-951b8dae1e11",
                                "text": "[…] si on est repéré de loin et que l'on se trouve dans un endroit bordé de murs par exemple, ou bien en terrain découvert, il n’y a pas d’échappatoire possible et gare à la fouille !…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "800b050a-129a-464c-90e5-01f90a664b0b",
                                "sense_id": "0d9e5229-00a4-314b-b399-951b8dae1e11",
                                "text": "Les chauffards vinrent rapidement à leur hauteur, les prirent en tenaille en les fracassant sur les côtés tandis que le troisième véhicule les bloquait par l'avant. Il n'y avait plus d’échappatoire possible […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b08ae93a-ebf9-33e2-859c-543c7662a56f",
                        "entry_id": "753cad07-f032-3995-a9fc-c4ae11d3edc6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Moyen de se décharger de quelque chose."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fcd0f503-57a5-4ee1-94f7-7066125b8fae",
                                "sense_id": "b08ae93a-ebf9-33e2-859c-543c7662a56f",
                                "text": "L’Action ? dit-il, mais ce n’est qu’une échappatoire où nous pousse notre paresse fuyant devant l’effort que demande le Rêve."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cabe16c-8c6b-43d0-aa4f-476e3c0f2b2c",
                                "sense_id": "b08ae93a-ebf9-33e2-859c-543c7662a56f",
                                "text": "D’une façon générale, je ne peux pas commencer à rédiger sans avoir auparavant accumulé une quantité phénoménale de notes, jusqu’à ce que cette accumulation devienne étouffante et que la rédaction apparaisse comme une échappatoire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f56c0be8-27b7-4a5b-a198-fdff0cd3da0f",
                                "sense_id": "b08ae93a-ebf9-33e2-859c-543c7662a56f",
                                "text": "« Les milliardaires ont tiré profit des échappatoires fiscales pour les riches, des suppressions fiscales pour les sociétés, des paradis fiscaux et de l’absence de taxes sur la richesse et les successions au Canada."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a7fac047-a97e-4f60-86c1-3df3d7543fd1",
                                "sense_id": "b08ae93a-ebf9-33e2-859c-543c7662a56f",
                                "text": "Dans ces régions, il sera possible de manger au resto avec un ami ou un proche, mais pas de le recevoir à la maison.\n « C’est une façon de donner une certaine échappatoire, ça peut être bon pour un couple. Le risque est moindre, tandis que ce qui se passe dans la maison, on est chez nous, la probabilité d’avoir des contacts est beaucoup plus grande », a-t-il dit."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f1edfd27-9a31-4dc2-b514-17e426441c0f",
                        "source_entry_id": "753cad07-f032-3995-a9fc-c4ae11d3edc6",
                        "source_sense_id": "0d9e5229-00a4-314b-b399-951b8dae1e11",
                        "source_sense_description": "Subterfuge",
                        "target_lang_word": "Ausweg",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Ausweg",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0921d6de-7b33-39cd-af94-f5d8e0a9f128",
                                        "entry_id": "fc9ec5a8-c85a-3a53-83c7-245ec7f41561",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Weg, der aus einem (meist unangenehmen oder gefährlichen) Ort hinausführt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e234d234-f9c2-4707-b9a5-ebae53c61d5b",
                                                "sense_id": "0921d6de-7b33-39cd-af94-f5d8e0a9f128",
                                                "text": "Ich bin im Wald verirrt! Gibt es hier denn keinen Ausweg?"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39d8c6c6-11b5-3809-b203-8991fba9df77",
                                        "entry_id": "fc9ec5a8-c85a-3a53-83c7-245ec7f41561",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lösung, die aus einer schwierigen Lage herausführt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "im übertragenen Sinne"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93ee19e5-13eb-4bd3-afde-5085e485ae56",
                                                "sense_id": "39d8c6c6-11b5-3809-b203-8991fba9df77",
                                                "text": "Der einzige Ausweg schien, ihr Kind bei Bekannten zu verstecken."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d8e6dbe-3c45-46aa-9a0c-10db41ddcab9",
                                                "sense_id": "39d8c6c6-11b5-3809-b203-8991fba9df77",
                                                "text": "„Im Streit um einen Ausweg aus der verfahrenen Lage bildeten sich zwei antagonistische Gruppierungen heraus.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "35b5b678-2750-4dac-bd91-dc931d7b81da",
                        "source_entry_id": "753cad07-f032-3995-a9fc-c4ae11d3edc6",
                        "source_sense_id": "0d9e5229-00a4-314b-b399-951b8dae1e11",
                        "source_sense_description": "Subterfuge",
                        "target_lang_word": "loophole",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "loophole",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "69551f97-ba9e-34ce-bf59-03c36c3da17c",
                                        "entry_id": "d0b7fa0b-20b9-3ed7-b0b8-a05534bacf5b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A slit in a castle wall; today, any similar window for shooting a ranged weapon or letting in light."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3c32130-cd56-4f1f-86be-fb0b7418ac8c",
                                                "sense_id": "69551f97-ba9e-34ce-bf59-03c36c3da17c",
                                                "text": "[…] and having a fair loophole, as it were, from a broken hole in the tree, he took a sure aim, without being seen, waiting till they were within about thirty yards of the tree, so that he could not miss."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b8ce0c3-e789-4d6a-9f79-caf382412eb0",
                                                "sense_id": "69551f97-ba9e-34ce-bf59-03c36c3da17c",
                                                "text": "There was a loophole in this wall, to let the light in, just at the height of a person's head, who was sitting near the chimney."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ed159bd-6de8-4648-962d-650dfb74f522",
                                                "sense_id": "69551f97-ba9e-34ce-bf59-03c36c3da17c",
                                                "text": "The sun had shifted round, and the myriad windows of the Ministry of Truth, with the light no longer shining on them, looked grim as the loopholes of a fortress."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0d23de02-144e-3193-b11c-5a24127736c1",
                                        "entry_id": "d0b7fa0b-20b9-3ed7-b0b8-a05534bacf5b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A method of escape, especially an ambiguity or exception in a rule or law that can be exploited in order to avoid its effect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0eee0b3-24bc-41be-8e36-1b8af5e4dc62",
                                                "sense_id": "0d23de02-144e-3193-b11c-5a24127736c1",
                                                "text": "Coupling the poor girl's intelligence with my previous knowledge, and the result of our good friend's inquiries on the spot, I left him no loophole of escape, and laid bare the whole villany which by these lights became plain as day."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b244412-4e9c-4069-8fba-b14cba115fb2",
                                                "sense_id": "0d23de02-144e-3193-b11c-5a24127736c1",
                                                "text": "You have a contract that says you will work until Island Towers is finalized, which I interpret as completion of construction, or I can stop you working elsewhere. And there's no loopholes, because you drafted it and you're the best."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2fb522f-181a-4c12-bb93-dafe3a1bfce4",
                                                "sense_id": "0d23de02-144e-3193-b11c-5a24127736c1",
                                                "text": "They would rather ask more from the vast majority of Americans and put our recovery at risk than close even a single tax loophole that benefits the wealthy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "loophole",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0cdfd1ac-6f97-3104-adbb-8c6dba7a9613",
                                        "entry_id": "6d6a753b-2607-3271-b5bb-a15bf657a014",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To prepare a building for defense by preparing slits or holes through which to fire on attackers"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12e9d469-8326-451d-866f-262c173b4dd0",
                                                "sense_id": "0cdfd1ac-6f97-3104-adbb-8c6dba7a9613",
                                                "text": "The lower windows were barricaded, and the whole building loopholed for musketry fire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "813c5578-2838-49ca-8d53-e8a7441d7225",
                                                "sense_id": "0cdfd1ac-6f97-3104-adbb-8c6dba7a9613",
                                                "text": "The doors were barricaded, the shutters closed upon the windows and loopholed, and provisions were brought in from the outhouses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43601d12-fcf0-44c7-bafe-9f48619fb644",
                                                "sense_id": "0cdfd1ac-6f97-3104-adbb-8c6dba7a9613",
                                                "text": "The Germans were loopholing it for defence."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7fa2fdb2-2591-3b08-b3af-037e29e9a520",
                                        "entry_id": "6d6a753b-2607-3271-b5bb-a15bf657a014",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To exploit (a law, etc.) by means of loopholes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3753f598-ceca-44b0-ac76-7eb92e0ba359",
                                                "sense_id": "7fa2fdb2-2591-3b08-b3af-037e29e9a520",
                                                "text": "Abroad they had developed loopholing the law into an art; in Israel they jettisoned loopholing for ignoring the law wherever possible. Obeying laws was for naive fools."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35fa063f-df87-4a74-8740-01bf79e76372",
                                                "sense_id": "7fa2fdb2-2591-3b08-b3af-037e29e9a520",
                                                "text": "De-moralizing the subject can be, quite simply, demoralizing, as stirring statements of ideals turn into persnickety rules with exceptions crying out to be loopholed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
